---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
	title="WATFA — Where are the free agents?"
	description="WATFA is a community-sourced open dataset of street dogs and cats in Guwahati."
	ogDescription="A public record of Guwahati's street dogs and cats."
	appendSiteName={false}
	mainClass="landing-main"
	skipHref="#overview"
	skipLabel="Skip to overview"
>
				<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
					<div class="hero-copy">
						<div class="hero-brand">
							<div class="hero-wordmark">
								<strong>WATFA</strong>
								<span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
								<p>Where are the<br />free agents?</p>
							</div>
							<p class="hero-focus">
								<span aria-hidden="true">⚠️</span>
								Currently: Guwahati only
							</p>
						</div>
						<h1 id="hero-title">
							A community-sourced public dataset of street dogs and cats, creating a shared, ongoing
							record of the free agents who live across our neighbourhoods.
						</h1>
						<a class="hero-community" href="https://chat.whatsapp.com/HdE6fLgzTei2yASyoAAUQZ?mode=gi_t">
							Join the community ↗
						</a>
					</div>

					<aside class="hero-how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
						<div class="card-head">
							<h2 id="how-title"><span class="card-number" aria-hidden="true">01 /</span> How it works</h2>
							<span class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">↘</span>
						</div>
						<div class="process-loop">
							<ol>
								<li>
									<div class="process-step-head"><span>01</span><strong>Record</strong></div>
									<p class="process-summary">
										If you spot a stray while out in your neighbourhood, you can record the sighting with a <strong>photo</strong>, the <strong>time</strong> and <strong>approximate location</strong>, plus
										any useful notes about their health, behaviour etc.
									</p>
									<div class="process-detail">
										<h3>Bootstrapping records</h3>
										<p>
Voluteers coordinate recurring recording sessions(weekly) in their neighbourhoods across the city, helping build the initial data for each area
and follow change over time.</p>
									</div>
								</li>
								<li>
									<div class="process-step-head"><span>02</span><strong>Index</strong></div>
									<p class="process-summary">
										Each sighting strengthens a shared index that people can search to learn whether an animal has been seen before, connect sightings over time and find possible matches for lost pets.
									</p>
									<div class="process-detail">
										<h3>Gets better with every sighting</h3>
										<p>
											WATFA organises photos, markings, locations and notes into searchable evidence. As more sightings are recorded, the index builds a richer picture of each animal and makes future search and matching more useful.
										</p>
									</div>
								</li>
							</ol>
							<div class="loop-return" aria-hidden="true"></div>
							<div class="loop-forward" aria-hidden="true"></div>
						</div>
					</aside>
				</section>

				<section class="poster-grid" id="overview" aria-label="More ways WATFA can help">
					<article class="card card-lost" aria-labelledby="lost-title">
						<div class="card-head">
							<h2 id="lost-title"><span class="card-number" aria-hidden="true">02 /</span> Lost &amp; Found</h2>
							<span class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">•••</span>
						</div>
						<ul class="card-points">
							<li>
								<span>
									<strong>Flag possible matches:</strong> A pet reported missing in Chandmari and an animal spotted on Zoo Road could be the same one.
									WATFA can flag the possible match and inform the pet’s owner.
								</span>
							</li>
							<li>
								<span>
									<strong>Keep reports together:</strong> Social media posts about lost&found are scattered and may not reach the right people. It's also difficult to maintain missing reports, sightings. In WATFA, all updates are kept together in one place.
								</span>
							</li>
							<li>
								<span>
									<strong>Widen the search:</strong> Search teams can also see other animals missing nearby and keep an eye out for them, not just
									the one they set out to find.
								</span>
							</li>
						</ul>
					</article>

					<article class="card card-search" aria-labelledby="search-title">
						<div class="card-head">
							<h2 id="search-title"><span class="card-number" aria-hidden="true">03 /</span> WATFA Search Party</h2>
							<span class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">▦</span>
						</div>
						<ul class="card-points">
							<li>
								<span>
									<strong>Build a local search network:</strong> Connect nearby people who can quickly spread the
									word, put up posters and help search when a pet goes missing.
								</span>
							</li>
							<li>
								<span>
									<strong>Coordinate searches better:</strong> Divide streets, track checked areas, document
									sightings, watch for multiple missing animals, and develop techniques and tools that make
									searches more efficient.
								</span>
							</li>
							<li>
								<span>
									<strong>Iterate on what works:</strong> Learn from each search and use those lessons to improve
									future search playbooks.
								</span>
							</li>
						</ul>
					</article>

					<article class="card card-research" aria-labelledby="research-title">
						<div class="card-head">
							<h2 id="research-title"><span class="card-number" aria-hidden="true">04 /</span> Research and analysis</h2>
							<span class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">◎</span>
						</div>
						<p>
							A long-running record of sightings could help researchers, civic bodies and animal-welfare
							groups understand how free-roaming animal populations change over time and plan where
							surveys, vaccination drives or other interventions may be most useful.
						</p>
						<div class="research-notes">
							<div class="research-note research-caution">
								<strong>Read with care.</strong>
								<span>Community observations have sampling bias. Record survey effort, missing data and confidence levels. Obscure sensitive locations. This is useful evidence, not an official count.</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</article>

					<article class="card card-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
						<div class="card-head">
							<h2 id="faq-title"><span class="card-number" aria-hidden="true">05 /</span> FAQ</h2>
							<span class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">?</span>
						</div>
						<dl class="faq-list">
							<div>
								<dt>Is this an app?</dt>
								<dd>
									No. WATFA is a community-sourced open public dataset. Not an app/platform/product. It may use forms, bots, a website or an app as its interface, but those
									can change.
								</dd>
							</div>
							<div>
								<dt>What about animal privacy?</dt>
								<dd>
									Precise locations help research and identification, but can also help thieves,
									smugglers or people trying to harm or illegally relocate animals. Public locations
									would stay fuzzy <strong>deliberately</strong>.
								</dd>
							</div>
							<div>
								<dt>Can WATFA help with animal rescue?</dt>
								<dd>
									Rescue is not WATFA's primary focus. If an animal is injured or in distress, use a
									dedicated service such as <a href="https://karunanidhan.app/">Karuna Nidhan</a>.
									We would rather integrate with existing rescue networks than replace or interfere
									with them.
								</dd>
							</div>
						</dl>
					</article>

					<article class="card card-help" id="help" aria-labelledby="help-title">
						<div class="card-head">
							<h2 id="help-title"><span class="card-number" aria-hidden="true">06 /</span> How to help</h2>
							<span class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">☰</span>
						</div>
						<dl>
							<div>
								<dt>Develop</dt>
								<dd>
                                    If you're a developer/designer we could use your help. We want help w developing the tools and services for recording sightings, identifying animals, mapping observations and searching.
                                    We need help with design, frontend, backend, data and computer vision.
									<a href="https://chat.whatsapp.com/LenDdTpSTKH0p4O3PjmfRF?s=sh&amp;p=a&amp;mlu=4&amp;ilr=4">Join the developer group ↗</a>
								</dd>
							</div>
							<div>
								<dt>Volunteer</dt>
								<dd>
									Join a recurring neighbourhood survey, photograph street animals and record when and where
									you saw them. You can also help organise surveys and verify existing records.
									<a href="https://chat.whatsapp.com/JHS9AzS31KmGpbKbhnpA7X?s=cl&amp;p=a&amp;mlu=4&amp;ilr=4">Join the volunteer group ↗</a>
								</dd>
							</div>
						</dl>
					</article>
				</section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
	.hero {
		display: grid;
		height: auto;
		min-height: max(560px, calc(65svh - 80px));
		grid-template-columns: 1.22fr 0.78fr;
		border-bottom: var(--line);
	}

	.hero-copy {
		display: flex;
		min-width: 0;
		flex-direction: column;
		justify-content: space-between;
		padding: clamp(24px, 3.5vw, 52px);
		border-right: var(--line);
	}

	.card-head {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 2;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
		gap: 16px;
		align-items: start;
		margin-bottom: clamp(14px, 1.6vw, 22px);
	}

	.card-head h2 {
		min-width: 0;
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--sans);
		font-size: var(--card-title-size);
		font-weight: 900;
		letter-spacing: -0.065em;
		line-height: 0.95;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.card-number {
		font-family: var(--mono);
		letter-spacing: -0.08em;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}

	.card-icon {
		margin-top: 0.2em;
		font: 700 1rem/1 var(--sans);
	}

	.hero-wordmark {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: clamp(10px, 1.4vw, 20px);
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.hero-wordmark strong {
		font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 5.8vw, 5rem);
		font-weight: 900;
		letter-spacing: -0.09em;
		line-height: 0.8;
	}

	.hero-wordmark > span {
		color: var(--orange);
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 3.5rem);
		font-weight: 300;
		line-height: 1;
	}

	.hero-wordmark p {
		margin: 0;
		font: 800 clamp(0.62rem, 0.9vw, 0.82rem)/1.08 var(--mono);
		letter-spacing: -0.04em;
	}

	.hero-focus {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 8px;
		width: fit-content;
		margin: 18px 0 0;
		padding: 8px 10px;
		background: var(--ink);
		color: var(--paper);
		font: 700 0.68rem/1.2 var(--mono);
		letter-spacing: 0.01em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.hero h1 {
		margin: auto 0;
		max-width: 760px;
		font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 3.1rem);
		font-weight: 500;
		letter-spacing: -0.045em;
		line-height: 1.02;
	}

	.hero-community {
		display: inline-flex;
		width: fit-content;
		padding: 11px 14px;
		border: var(--line);
		background: var(--ink);
		color: white;
		font: 800 0.72rem/1 var(--mono);
		text-decoration: none;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.hero-community:hover,
	.hero-community:focus-visible {
		background: var(--ink);
	}

	.hero-how {
		display: flex;
		min-width: 0;
		flex-direction: column;
		padding: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 34px);
		background: var(--blue);
		color: white;
	}

	.process-loop {
		position: relative;
	}

	.hero-how ol {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-rows: repeat(2, 1fr);
		gap: 8px;
		margin: 0 25px;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}

	.hero-how li {
		display: flex;
		min-height: 0;
		flex-direction: column;
		padding: clamp(9px, 1.3vw, 15px);
		border: 1px solid white;
	}

	.process-step-head {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 30px 1fr;
		gap: 10px;
		align-items: baseline;
	}

	.process-step-head span {
		font: 700 var(--card-label-size) var(--mono);
		color: var(--lime);
	}

	.process-step-head strong {
		font-family: var(--sans);
		font-size: var(--card-subheading-size);
		font-weight: 800;
		line-height: 1.1;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.process-summary {
		max-width: 66ch;
		margin: 8px 0 13px 40px;
		font-family: var(--sans);
		font-size: var(--card-body-size);
		line-height: var(--card-body-leading);
	}

	.process-summary strong {
		padding: 0.08em 0.3em;
		background: var(--lime);
		color: var(--ink);
		font-weight: 800;
		-webkit-box-decoration-break: clone;
		box-decoration-break: clone;
	}

	.process-detail {
		margin-top: auto;
		padding: 11px 0 0 40px;
		border-top: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 55%);
	}

	.process-detail h3 {
		margin: 0 0 5px;
		color: var(--lime);
		font: 800 var(--card-label-size)/1.25 var(--mono);
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.process-detail p {
		max-width: 68ch;
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--sans);
		font-size: var(--card-note-size);
		font-weight: 500;
		line-height: var(--card-note-leading);
	}

	.loop-return,
	.loop-forward {
		position: absolute;
		top: 25%;
		bottom: 25%;
		width: 26px;
	}

	.loop-return {
		left: 0;
		border-top: 2px solid var(--lime);
		border-bottom: 2px solid var(--lime);
		border-left: 2px solid var(--lime);
	}

	.loop-return::before {
		position: absolute;
		top: -5px;
		right: -1px;
		width: 0;
		height: 0;
		border-top: 4px solid transparent;
		border-bottom: 4px solid transparent;
		border-left: 7px solid var(--lime);
		content: "";
	}

	.loop-forward {
		right: 0;
		border-top: 2px solid var(--lime);
		border-right: 2px solid var(--lime);
		border-bottom: 2px solid var(--lime);
	}

	.loop-forward::after {
		position: absolute;
		bottom: -5px;
		left: -1px;
		width: 0;
		height: 0;
		border-top: 4px solid transparent;
		border-right: 7px solid var(--lime);
		border-bottom: 4px solid transparent;
		content: "";
	}

	.poster-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		scroll-margin-top: 10px;
	}

	.card {
		--card-pad: clamp(20px, 2.5vw, 36px);
		position: relative;
		min-width: 0;
		min-height: 320px;
		padding: var(--card-pad);
		border-right: var(--line);
		border-bottom: var(--line);
		overflow: hidden;
	}

	.card:nth-child(2n) { border-right: 0; }

	.card p,
	.card dd {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 2;
		font-family: var(--sans);
		font-size: var(--card-body-size);
		line-height: var(--card-body-leading);
	}

	.card p { margin-bottom: 8px; }
	.card strong { font-weight: 800; }

	.card-lost {
		display: flex;
		min-height: 390px;
		flex-direction: column;
		background: var(--lost);
		color: white;
	}

	.card-points {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 2;
		display: grid;
		max-width: 68ch;
		margin: clamp(2px, 0.5vw, 8px) 0 0;
		padding: 0;
		font-family: var(--sans);
		font-size: clamp(0.9rem, 0.82rem + 0.28vw, 1.05rem);
		font-weight: 450;
		letter-spacing: -0.018em;
		line-height: 1.4;
		list-style: none;
	}

	.card-points li {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 12px minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: clamp(10px, 1vw, 15px);
		padding: clamp(11px, 1vw, 15px) 0;
		border-top: var(--line);
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}

	.card-lost .card-points li { border-color: rgb(255 255 255 / 38%); }

	.card-points li::before {
		width: 8px;
		height: 8px;
		margin-top: 0.48em;
		background: var(--lime);
		content: "";
	}

	.card-search { background: var(--paper); }
	.card-search .card-points li::before { background: var(--ink); }

	.card-research {
		display: flex;
		min-height: 370px;
		flex-direction: column;
		background: var(--blue);
		color: white;
	}

	.research-notes {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 3;
		margin: auto calc(-1 * var(--card-pad)) calc(-1 * var(--card-pad));
		padding-top: 20px;
	}

	.research-note {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(92px, auto) 1fr;
		gap: 12px;
		align-items: start;
		padding: 11px var(--card-pad);
		border-top: 1px solid white;
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	.research-caution { background: var(--lime); }

	.research-note strong {
		font-family: var(--sans);
		font-size: var(--card-note-size);
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.research-note span {
		font-family: var(--sans);
		font-size: var(--card-note-size);
		line-height: var(--card-note-leading);
	}

	.research-note b { font-weight: 800; }

	.card-faq {
		display: flex;
		min-height: 370px;
		flex-direction: column;
		background: var(--yellow);
	}

	.faq-list {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 2;
		margin: auto 0 0;
	}

	.faq-list > div {
		padding-top: clamp(14px, 2vw, 24px);
		border-top: var(--line);
	}

	.faq-list dt {
		margin-bottom: 12px;
		font-family: var(--sans);
		font-size: var(--card-subheading-size);
		font-weight: 800;
		letter-spacing: -0.04em;
		line-height: 1.1;
	}

	.faq-list dd {
		max-width: 62ch;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.card-help {
		display: flex;
		min-height: 230px;
		grid-column: 1 / -1;
		flex-direction: column;
		border-right: 0;
		border-bottom: 0;
		scroll-margin-top: 10px;
	}

	.card-help dl {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		margin: auto 0 0;
	}

	.card-help dl > div {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: max-content minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 10px;
		padding: 12px clamp(12px, 1.5vw, 22px);
		border-top: var(--line);
		border-right: var(--line);
	}

	.card-help dl > div:first-child { padding-left: 0; }
	.card-help dl > div:last-child { padding-right: 0; border-right: 0; }

	.card-help dt {
		font-family: var(--sans);
		font-size: var(--card-subheading-size);
		font-weight: 800;
		line-height: 1.1;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.card-help dd {
		display: grid;
		gap: 10px;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.card-help dd a {
		width: fit-content;
		color: inherit;
		font-weight: 700;
		text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
	}

	@media (max-width: 900px) {
		.hero {
			height: auto;
			min-height: 0;
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.hero-copy { min-height: 500px; border-right: 0; border-bottom: var(--line); }
		.hero-how { min-height: 0; }
		.poster-grid {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		}

		.card { min-height: 260px; border-right: var(--line); border-bottom: var(--line); }
		.card:nth-child(2n) { border-right: 0; }
		.card-help { min-height: 220px; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 0; }
		.card-help dl > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
	}

	@media (max-width: 560px) {
		.hero-copy { min-height: 480px; padding: 24px 16px; }
		.hero-wordmark { gap: 8px; }
		.hero-wordmark strong { font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 13vw, 4rem); }
		.hero-wordmark > span { font-size: 1.8rem; }
		.hero-wordmark p { font-size: clamp(0.55rem, 2.6vw, 0.7rem); }
		.hero h1 { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 7vw, 2.5rem); }
		.hero-how { min-height: 0; padding: 20px 16px; }
		.card-head h2 { font-size: 1.75rem; }

		.poster-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
		.card,
		.card:nth-child(2n),
		.card-help {
			--card-pad: 17px;
			grid-column: auto;
			grid-row: auto;
			min-height: 235px;
			padding: var(--card-pad);
			border-right: 0;
			border-bottom: var(--line);
		}

		.card-help { border-bottom: 0; }
		.card-lost { min-height: 370px; }
		.card-research, .card-faq { min-height: 360px; }
		.card-help { min-height: 300px; }
		.card-help dl { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
		.card-help dl > div {
			grid-template-columns: max-content minmax(0, 1fr);
			padding: 10px 0;
			border-right: 0;
		}
	}
</style>
